{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "697dca02-0f30-45ca-8a88-381324906e0c",
    "name": "Program Capacity & Invoice Reservation API",
    "description": "HTTP API for the Program Capacity & Invoice Reservation POC service: Programs, Invoices, Reservations, and Releases, plus JWT authentication and health checks.\n\nTreasury reconciliation is consumed exclusively through Kafka (the `treasury.reconciliation` topic) and is intentionally NOT represented here as an HTTP request — no reconciliation HTTP endpoint exists in this service. See the project README for how to exercise that flow by publishing a Kafka message directly.\n\nWorkflow: Register or Login -> Create Program -> Create Invoice -> Create Reservation -> Get Program (reduced availability) -> Release Reservation -> Get Program (restored availability). Run requests top-to-bottom against the `Local` environment; each request that creates a resource automatically stores its id/token(s) into environment variables consumed by later requests.\n\nAuthorization is configured at the collection level as a Bearer token using `{{accessToken}}`; public routes (register/login/refresh/health/readiness, plus the two negative-auth examples in Failure Scenarios) override this with No Auth.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [],
  "variable": [],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Process liveness only. Public — no JWT required. Always returns 200 while the Node process is up, independent of PostgreSQL/Kafka availability.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {\n  pm.response.to.have.status(200);\n});",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () {\n  pm.response.to.be.json;\n});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/readiness",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "readiness"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Process liveness + PostgreSQL reachability. Public — no JWT required. Returns 200 when PostgreSQL is reachable, 503 otherwise.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is one of [200,503]', function () {\n  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200,503]);\n});",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () {\n  pm.response.to.be.json;\n});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Creates a User and immediately issues a token pair. Re-running this with the same `userEmail` returns 409 Conflict (duplicate email) — use Login instead once the demo user already exists.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {\n  pm.response.to.have.status(201);\n});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();\n\nif (body.user && body.user.id) {\n  pm.environment.set('userId', body.user.id);\n}\nif (body.access_token) {\n  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.access_token);\n}\nif (body.refresh_token) {\n  pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);\n}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Exchanges email/password for a fresh access/refresh token pair. Use this on any run after the demo user already exists.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {\n  pm.response.to.have.status(200);\n});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();\n\nif (body.access_token) {\n  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.access_token);\n}\nif (body.refresh_token) {\n  pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);\n}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Authenticated by the refresh token itself, sent as `refresh_token` in the JSON body (NOT as a Bearer header — this endpoint uses a dedicated refresh-token guard/strategy, mirroring the actual `JwtRefreshStrategy` body-field extractor). Rotation is implemented: the old refresh token is invalidated and both tokens in the environment are replaced with the newly issued pair.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {\n  pm.response.to.have.status(200);\n});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();\n\nif (body.access_token) {\n  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.access_token);\n}\nif (body.refresh_token) {\n  pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);\n}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Current User (Me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Protected by the global access-token guard (inherits collection Bearer auth). Returns the normalized `AuthenticatedUser` shape resolved from the access token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {\n  pm.response.to.have.status(200);\n});",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () {\n  pm.response.to.be.json;\n});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
